<mxCell id="authors-ca-note" value="Adoption of Clean Architecture pattern" style="shape=note;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;size=14;fillColor=#A9DDF3;strokeColor=#000000;fontSize=10;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="1680" y="40" width="180" height="40" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
<mxCell id="authors-b-legend" value="Authors broken into its business capabilities. Grey lines: the Authors API delegates to each capability.&lt;br&gt;Each capability's own ports show which other subdomains it needs.&lt;br&gt;Since the base project, AuthorController no longer imports ReaderDetails and User." style="shape=note;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;size=14;fillColor=#A9DDF3;strokeColor=#000000;fontSize=10;align=left;spacingLeft=6;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="100" y="1310" width="690" height="110" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
<mxCell id="authors-a-legend" value="Ball-and-socket and dashed arrows: each layer depends on the one below, as in Clean Architecture.&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Thick lines&lt;/b&gt;: the layer uses another module's repositories or domain classes, not its API.&lt;br&gt;&lt;font color='#E06666'&gt;&lt;b&gt;Soft red&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/font&gt;: violation (another module's internals, an external system reached from inside the core, or a dependency pointing outwards).&lt;br&gt;Not drawn: every layer uses the Exceptions Module.&lt;br&gt;Kept from the base project: Interface Adapters also use the EBR API directly.&lt;br&gt;Red dashed arrow: services and repositories still use an api view (AuthorLendingView). Fixed since the base project: Author no longer uses UpdateAuthorRequest." style="shape=note;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;size=14;fillColor=#A9DDF3;strokeColor=#000000;fontSize=10;align=left;spacingLeft=6;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="830" y="1310" width="1070" height="110" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
<mxCell id="authors-i-legend" value="Dashed grey boxes: template elements with no counterpart in the package.&lt;br&gt;&lt;font color='#E06666'&gt;&lt;b&gt;Soft red&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/font&gt;: violation. Red dashed arrows point outwards, against the dependency rule.&lt;br&gt;Not marked: BookViewMapper and the Book views (borderline: Book's REST adapter code).&lt;br&gt;AuthorService returns Book entities, so Book leaks into the controllers. Author has no lending data of its own:&lt;br&gt;the top-5 query joins the Book and Lending tables. Domain classes carry JPA annotations." style="shape=note;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;size=14;fillColor=#A9DDF3;strokeColor=#000000;fontSize=10;align=left;spacingLeft=6;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="2000" y="1310" width="1890" height="110" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
