<mxCell id="lendings-hdr-0" value="Business Logic View" style="shape=note;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;size=14;fillColor=#A9DDF3;strokeColor=#000000;fontSize=10;fontSize=11;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="340" y="40" width="160" height="40" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
<mxCell id="lendings-hdr-1" value="Architecture Logic View" style="shape=note;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;size=14;fillColor=#A9DDF3;strokeColor=#000000;fontSize=10;fontSize=11;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="1490" y="40" width="160" height="40" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
<mxCell id="lendings-hdr-2" value="Implementation View" style="shape=note;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;size=14;fillColor=#A9DDF3;strokeColor=#000000;fontSize=10;fontSize=11;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="3075" y="40" width="160" height="40" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
<mxCell id="lendings-ca-note" value="Adoption of Clean Architecture pattern" style="shape=note;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;size=14;fillColor=#A9DDF3;strokeColor=#000000;fontSize=10;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="1680" y="40" width="180" height="40" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
<mxCell id="lendings-b-legend" value="Lendings broken into its business capabilities. Grey lines: the Lendings API delegates to each capability.&lt;br&gt;New since the base project: renewal, per-reader lending policies, and the lending events that Notifications listens to.&lt;br&gt;The 'own lendings only' checks are still done in LendingController, not in a service." style="shape=note;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;size=14;fillColor=#A9DDF3;strokeColor=#000000;fontSize=10;align=left;spacingLeft=6;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="100" y="1610" width="690" height="110" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
<mxCell id="lendings-a-legend" value="Ball-and-socket and dashed arrows: each layer depends on the one below, as in Clean Architecture.&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Thick lines&lt;/b&gt;: the layer uses another module's repositories or domain classes, not its API.&lt;br&gt;&lt;font color='#E06666'&gt;&lt;b&gt;Soft red&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/font&gt;: violation (another module's internals, an external system reached from inside the core, or a dependency pointing outwards).&lt;br&gt;Not drawn: every layer uses the Exceptions Module.&lt;br&gt;Kept from the base project: Interface Adapters also use the EBR API directly.&lt;br&gt;New since the base project: the policy and event packages of Enterprise Business Rules are framework-free (ArchUnit). Events leave through Spring's ApplicationEventPublisher; the module never depends on Notifications." style="shape=note;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;size=14;fillColor=#A9DDF3;strokeColor=#000000;fontSize=10;align=left;spacingLeft=6;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="830" y="1610" width="1070" height="110" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
<mxCell id="lendings-i-legend" value="Dashed grey boxes: template elements with no counterpart in the package.&lt;br&gt;&lt;font color='#E06666'&gt;&lt;b&gt;Soft red&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/font&gt;: violation. Red dashed arrows point outwards, against the dependency rule.&lt;br&gt;Kept from the base project: Controllers use Domain directly; Services use Repositories.&lt;br&gt;LendingServiceImpl still bypasses BookService and ReaderService. Configuration binds LendingPolicyProperties.&lt;br&gt;Lending, LendingNumber and Fine carry JPA annotations; the policy and event classes do not." style="shape=note;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;size=14;fillColor=#A9DDF3;strokeColor=#000000;fontSize=10;align=left;spacingLeft=6;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="2000" y="1610" width="1890" height="110" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
